cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HES: multi-objective sizing of hybrid renewable energy systems"
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Roshandel
    given-names: Emad
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/emadroshandel/Hybrid_Energy_System"
abstract: >-
  An open-source application for the optimal sizing of hybrid renewable
  energy systems. Twenty generation, storage and demand technologies are
  dispatched hour by hour over a full year and sized by multi-objective
  optimisation, returning a Pareto front rather than a single design. The
  modelling chain comprises the NOAA solar position, the Erbs decomposition,
  the Hay-Davies transposition and the Faiman cell temperature for the
  photovoltaic path; shear, air-density and power-curve models for wind; a
  symmetric-efficiency state-of-charge model with throughput and calendar
  ageing for storage; an affine fuel curve with a minimum load ratio for
  dispatchable plant; and a two-state Markov representation of supply
  interruptions. Net present cost, levelised cost of energy, loss of power
  supply probability, renewable fraction and emissions are evaluated on a
  present-worth basis, and a plausibility layer checks every input and every
  result against published ranges. Runs locally as a desktop or browser
  application, or entirely in the browser via Pyodide.
